# Development defaults for uv-managed xpool commands.
#
# Use this file by copying it to a local .env and editing local-only values.
# Canonical pytest commands and the pre-commit pytest hook conditionally set
# UV_ENV_FILE to this repository-root file when it exists. For other uv commands,
# set UV_ENV_FILE explicitly:
#
#   export UV_ENV_FILE="$PWD/.env"
#   uv run xpool daemon check
#
# Keep the real .env untracked.

XPOOL_CONFIG=configs/dev.local.toml

# CUDA MPS is required for daemon readiness and production transport. Replace
# REPLACE_UID with a host-unique value, create both directories, and start the
# MPS control daemon before launching xpool. These variables select an existing
# controller; they do not start one.
# CUDA_MPS_PIPE_DIRECTORY=/tmp/xpool-mps-REPLACE_UID/pipe
# CUDA_MPS_LOG_DIRECTORY=/tmp/xpool-mps-REPLACE_UID/log
# Start the controller with every GPU visible to PyTorch clients. The MPS
# server starts lazily when the first agent or SGLang CUDA client connects:
#
#   mkdir -p /tmp/xpool-mps-REPLACE_UID/{pipe,log}
#   export UV_ENV_FILE="$PWD/.env"
#   CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES="$(nvidia-smi --query-gpu=uuid --format=csv,noheader | paste -sd, -)" \
#     uv run nvidia-cuda-mps-control -d
#   printf 'get_default_active_thread_percentage\n' | uv run nvidia-cuda-mps-control

# Limit local CUDA compilation and device linking to the installed GPU. This
# host-specific override keeps CMake's broad release architecture default intact.
# A100 uses 80; select the compute capability for the local development GPU.
# CMAKE_ARGS=-DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=80

# Create an ignored configs/dev.local.toml for host-specific devices and model
# paths. Model ids such as deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V2-Lite-Chat resolve through
# [vendor].model_base_uri unless a model entry provides an explicit absolute
# path override.

# Loopback is enabled together with exactly one execution site: instance,
# atnagent, or ffnagent. The FfnAgent site is reserved until the
# cross-agent transport runtime is implemented.
# XPOOL_DEBUG_LOOPBACK_ENABLE=1
# XPOOL_DEBUG_LOOPBACK_SITE=atnagent
#
# Graph observer variables are normally injected by tests that need them. Set
# them manually only for ad hoc SGLang graph debugging.
# XPOOL_DEBUG_GRAPH_OBSERVER_ENABLE=1
# XPOOL_DEBUG_GRAPH_OBSERVER_OUTDIR=.xpool-cache/graph-observer
#
# Native transport phase observation is disabled by default because it writes
# device timestamps for every request. Enable both settings for diagnostics.
# XPOOL_DEBUG_TRANSPORT_OBSERVER_ENABLE=1
# XPOOL_DEBUG_TRANSPORT_OBSERVER_OUTDIR=.xpool-cache/transport-observer

# SGLang loads xpool from the sglang.srt.plugins entry point group.
SGLANG_PLUGINS=xpool
